FusionSpace HPR · Sim simulates the flights of hobby and high-power rockets.

Every command prints text, or one JSON document with --json. Run a command marked "not available yet" and it names the milestone that brings it.

Usage: hpr [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  sim          Fly a design (.ork, .hpr, .hprz or a rocket's .json) off a rail and print its flight; save its recording with --export
  convert      Convert a motor file between .eng and .rse, write a catalog motor as either, or convert a design between .ork, .hpr and .hprz
  motors       Look up motors in the bundled catalog, read a .eng or .rse motor file, fetch a curve from ThrustCurve.org, or search vendors' stock and prices
  weather      Fetch a launch day's weather, or read a weather file, as a profile of air and wind
  mc           Fly a design many times with its inputs scattered at random, and print how its apogee and landing spread; save every flight with --export
  optimize     Search a design's parameters for a goal (not available yet)
  compare      Compare a flight log with its simulation (not available yet)
  analyze      Read a flight log and print its readings, with no design file
  diagnose     Diagnose what went wrong in a flight from its log (not available yet)
  completions  Print a shell completion script for `hpr`
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --json
          Print one JSON document on standard output instead of text, errors included

      --color <WHEN>
          When to use color. With auto, output to a terminal is colored, and NO_COLOR, FORCE_COLOR and CLICOLOR_FORCE are followed. JSON output never has color
          
          [default: auto]
          [possible values: auto, always, never]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Examples:
  Fly a design on the motor it was saved with:
      hpr sim my-rocket.ork
  Fly it on another motor, in a 4 m/s wind from the west:
      hpr sim my-rocket.ork --motor H170M --delay 10 --wind 4 --wind-from 270
  Work out a catalog motor's impulse, thrust and burn time:
      hpr motors show H170M

Guide: https://hpr.fusionspace.co/cli.html
